## 6. return to STOP a function early

`return;` with no value just **stops** the function. This is used for **input checks**:

```js
function tippel() {
  let t = Number(document.getElementById("tipp").value);

  if (t < 1 || t > 100) {
    document.getElementById("valasz").innerHTML = "1 és 100 közötti számot adj meg!";
    return;                 // STOP here, the rest doesn't run
  }

  // this part only runs if the input was OK
  db = db + 1;
  ...
}
```

> 💡 Pattern: **check first, `return` if it's bad, do the real work after.** It saves you from big nested `if`s.

