## 14. Functions calling other functions

A function can call another function, so you don't write the same code twice:

```js
function tippel() {
  // checks the guess ...
}

function kattint() {
  document.getElementById("tipp").value = aktualis;  // put the ruler number in the input
  tippel();                                          // reuse the guess logic
}
```

Small helper functions keep the main one clean:

```js
function hiba(szoveg) {
  document.getElementById("eredmeny").innerHTML = "<span class='hiba'>" + szoveg + "</span>";
}

function valt() {
  if (nev == "")   { hiba("Add meg a neved!"); return; }
  if (osszeg <= 0) { hiba("Az összeg legyen pozitív!"); return; }
  ...
}
```

### Running something at page load

```js
function indit() { ... }

indit();     // called once at the end of the script -> runs when the page opens
```

