## 15. Functions as values (callbacks)

In JavaScript a function is a **value**, like a number. You can store it, and you can **give it to another function**. A function you pass in like this is called a **callback**.

```js
function kiir(szoveg) {
  alert(szoveg);
}

function ketszer(muvelet) {     // muvelet will be a function
  muvelet("első");
  muvelet("második");
}

ketszer(kiir);                  // pass the function (no brackets!)
```

Where you'll meet callbacks:

```js
setTimeout(function () { alert("2 másodperc letelt"); }, 2000);   // run once after 2000 ms

let ora = setInterval(() => { console.log("tick"); }, 1000);      // run every 1000 ms
clearInterval(ora);                                                // stop it

[1, 2, 3].forEach(function (szam) { console.log(szam * 10); });   // 10, 20, 30

document.querySelectorAll("td").forEach(td => td.style.color = "red");
```

