## 16. Built-in functions you already use

These are functions too. Someone else declared them, and you just call them:

| Call | Gives back |
|---|---|
| `alert("x")` | nothing (shows a popup) |
| `prompt("Név?")` | the typed text |
| `confirm("Biztos?")` | `true` / `false` |
| `Number("12")` | `12` |
| `parseInt("12.7")` | `12` |
| `Math.random()` | random 0 … 0.999 |
| `Math.floor(4.9)` | `4` |
| `Math.round(4.5)` | `5` |
| `isNaN(x)` | `true` if x is not a number |
| `document.getElementById("id")` | the HTML element |
| `console.log(x)` | nothing (prints to F12 console) |
| `szam.toFixed(2)` | text with 2 decimals |
| `szoveg.replace(".", ",")` | the new text |

> 💡 Ones with a dot (`Math.floor`, `szam.toFixed`) are **methods**: functions that belong to something.

