## 18. Common mistakes

| Mistake | What happens | Fix |
|---|---|---|
| `function tippel { }` | syntax error | brackets are required: `function tippel() { }` |
| `tippel;` | nothing runs | `tippel();` |
| `onclick="tippel"` | nothing runs | `onclick="tippel()"` |
| `addEventListener("click", tippel())` | runs at page load, not on click | `addEventListener("click", tippel)` |
| No `return` | result is `undefined` | `return a + b;` |
| Code after `return` | never runs | move it above the return |
| `let` variable inside func, used in another func | "is not defined" | declare it outside, at the top |
| `let titok = ...` inside `indit()` when `titok` is global | the global stays empty | drop `let`: `titok = ...` |
| `Tippel()` vs `tippel()` | "is not defined" | same capitals everywhere |
| Missing `}` | "Unexpected end of input" | count `{` and `}`, they must match |
| `mozog()` for a mouse handler | `event` is undefined | `onmousemove="mozog(event)"` + `function mozog(event)` |
| Calling an arrow/expression before its line | "Cannot access before initialization" | move the declaration up, or use `function` |
| `"5" + "3"` inside function = `"53"` | inputs are text | `Number(...)` before math |

